ntifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/init(_:)-4kjv4"]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-4kjv4":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The one hypergraph conversion for a type that is both a graph and a hypergraph: read as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/init(_:)-4kjv4","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4kjv4","title":"init(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"role":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"role":"collection","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set of vertices of any size, the empty set included (Berge, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hypergraphs"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 1989). Not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no shared parent with one: a hyperedge is not an edge. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" module’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidenceGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a hypergraph as its bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how the graph algorithms reach it."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","title":"Hypergraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]}}}